 first time we see wanda it's  pretty much revealed that she is the  villain there's no fighting there's no  beheading but the next time we see her  she pretty much takes down the whole  camera tag and she kills a bunch of  innocent sorcerers so this scene would  have been pretty cool but it was pretty  well established from the beginning of  the movie that wanda was indeed the  villain and since they didn't actually  show this scene this leaves it open for  doctor strange 3 for morta to return so  this story could be further explored and  developed now that scene is dark in a  killing type of way but this next  deleted scene is dark on a different  level and it would have set the  illuminati up to be more of antagonists  of the film than they actually were this  was revealed by moviescope.com where  they say in the original cut of the  movie this wanda storyline was probably  the darkest thing marvel studios had  ever done in an mcu film and what  they're actually referring to is the  origin story of the wanda from the 838  universe the wanda in the illuminati's  universe in which our wanda uses to  dreamwalk now if you recall in the movie  mordo mentions to doctor strange when he  arrives in a sanctum that he had the  darkhold and that wanda could do  something far worse which was  dreamwalking so mordo knew about  dreamwalking which means that 838  universe doctor strange most likely knew  about it too and according to this  deleted scene he definitely did and the  whole illuminati did too and they  decided to attack wanda before she had  the chance to attack anybody else  according to moviescope.com they say  originally when the doctor strange  variant of that universe encounters the  darkhold he also came across the chapter  that detailed the scarlet witch prophecy  this page of course was shown to us in  one division by agatha harkness they  also reiterated it in multiverse of  madness where they said she was made to  either rule the entire multiverse or  destroy it that's the prophecy of the  scarlet witch so doctor strange of that  universe came across it and he informed  the illuminati of his findings and they  all came to the conclusion of performing  a lobotomy on their universe's wanda so  as to prevent the prophecy from ever  happening in that universe now for those  who don't know what a lobotomy is it's a  form of brain surgery that involves  severing connections in the brain's  prefrontal cortex so it's a pretty big  deal and pretty dang dark but the  article continues to say this lobotomy  would be performed by none other than  their resident telepath charles xavier  who was meant to remove wanda's access  to her abilities thus creating the  domestic wanda variant and perhaps they  actually did this because i'm sure most  people noticed the wanda in that  universe was way weaker than the wanda  in our universe when arwanda came in she  pretty much wiped the floor with her and  when she was dream walking in that body  it's safe to say that some of her powers  kind of transferred over so this would  describe more of that tame wanda however  this isn't the end of the scene they say  that in order to perform this lobotomy  they needed to consult wanda's  biological father which is where the  deleted scene with michael fassbender as  magneto would have come into play now  over the past couple of days it was  revealed that there were five cameos  that were actually shot but were cut  from the final version of the movie and  one of those cameos was said to be  michael fassbender's magneto and  according to movie scope this was the  scene that was shot and filmed now of  course this is kind of a darker story  but this is really really exciting  because they were going to acknowledge  that at one point in time in the comics  magneto is the biological father of  wanda now what's interesting is that it  doesn't say that magneto was going to be  a part of the illuminati like some of  the other cameos for example a scene  